page('Literature synthesis');h('3.1 Synthesis and precise candidate distinction')
para('Detection literature [1-4] separates unusual observations from diagnosis. An anomalous reading is not proof of harmful behavior, and a normal reading under throttling is not proof of recovery. The current small evaluation measures classification error; it does not validate restoration decisions.')
para('Latency-aware allocation [5-12], resource accounting and cluster management [13-18], and approximation-based control [19] show that monitoring, allocation changes and protected-service objectives are mature ideas. Scheduler designs [20-21] also demonstrate why control timing and actuator semantics matter.')
para('Breakwater [22] is particularly relevant because speculative additional credits can reveal unmet demand. FIRM, Sinan and Sage [23-25] establish telemetry-driven resource correction and learned diagnosis. Combining probing, ML and a latency threshold is therefore not a sufficient novelty argument.')
table(['Candidate detail','Evidence and remaining question'],[['Repeated A-B-A windows','Implemented in recovery_probe.py; compare exact protocols and claim language with full prior-art disclosures.'],['Grant-normalized CPU consumption','Implemented demand gate. Blocking, contention and multicore behavior can still confound interpretation.'],['Restoration before decision','Implemented cleanup ordering; ordinary rollback and defensive cleanup are established techniques.'],['Combined stability contract','Identity, validity, load, drift and latency gates are implemented. Whether this conjunction is inventive remains unresolved.']],[190,318])
para('The defensible research question is whether this particular contract reduces premature release relative to the legacy recovery rule under changing demand. A representative live experiment and ablations are needed; no claim of superiority over the 25 published systems is made.')

page('Summary');h('4. Summary of the invention:')
para('ARQ is an operating-systems prototype that observes process telemetry and applies graduated execution restrictions. Its original recovery rule accepts repeated low anomaly readings as evidence for stepping down restrictions. That can be misleading: the restriction itself may have reduced the observed CPU usage while the process still wants more execution time.')
para('The research extension tests one proposed increase from a restricted allocation A to a larger allocation B. Each release window B is bracketed by restricted control windows A. The runner checks measurement validity, process incarnation, offered-load stability, control-window latency drift, protected-service latency and CPU consumption relative to the larger grant. It reapplies A before committing a successful result. A failed or inconclusive experiment retains the restriction.')
h('Technical problem and effect');para('The technical problem is premature relaxation based on controller-suppressed observations. The intended effect is more selective CPU-duty relaxation using additional experimental evidence. Regression tests and an explicit synthetic model support the implemented logic. Live benefits of this bracketed policy, production safety and generalization are not established.')
h('Scope and current implementation');para('The bracketed runner and throttler adapter are implemented as an opt-in research API. They are separate from default dashboard restoration. Supporting work includes process-level detector evaluation, a support-aware candidate and guarded optional ML assistance. A new Kaggle study trains server-level Isolation Forest and Extra Trees models on 94,526 cleaned unique observations. Its collection domains are confounded with labels, and its features cannot replace the live process model. These studies do not establish the novelty of the bracketed protocol.')
para('This document is a technical disclosure draft. It is not a filed application or a patent grant. Team membership does not establish legal inventorship; actual human conception, AI assistance and institutional ownership require confirmation.')
page('Objectives');h('5. Objectives of the invention:')
for i,t in enumerate(['Verify one proposed relaxation of an existing CPU restriction using repeated A-B-A observation groups.','Distinguish low restricted usage from continued saturation of a larger temporary grant.','Check the protected workload against absolute and relative p95 latency bounds.','Treat offered-load changes, control drift and invalid observations as inconclusive rather than recovered.','Reserve a nominal incremental execution allowance before actuation and restore the original restriction before deciding.','Retain phase observations, outcomes and rejection reasons in a trace.','Provide reproducible tests and labelled evaluation while keeping unvalidated ML out of automatic control.'],1):para(str(i)+'. '+t)
h('Measurable outcomes');para('Observe whether a candidate is accepted or rejected, the reason, final requested duty and recorded nominal allowance. For detector evaluation, report confusion counts, precision, recall, F1, false-positive/negative rates and agreement with rule decisions. For repeated live trials, report measured processing-time percentiles and throughput with sample variability.')
para('A lower score, fewer flags or one passing experiment is not evidence of global optimality or general recovery. Application data integrity, multicore demand, memory isolation and unobserved workload phases need separate testing.')
page('Components');h('6. Components and Working Principle:')
table(['Module','Function','Source location'],[['Process monitor','Native telemetry and process-incarnation cache reset.','arq/core/monitor.py'],['Rule scorer / restoration','Resource scoring and original hysteresis transitions.','arq/core/'],['Duty actuator','Stop/continue pulsing with cleanup.','quarantine_controller.py'],['RecoveryProbe','Bracketed experiment and acceptance gates.','recovery_probe.py'],['Window / ProbePolicy','Observation contract and configured limits.','recovery_probe.py'],['Throttler adapter','Change an already restricted duty allocation.','recovery_probe.py'],['Guarded ML path','Validated soft-restriction corroboration; managed-child and dry-run controls.','ml_policy.py; guarded_controller.py'],['Evaluation tools','Labelled data, repeated fits and randomized-order live trials.','arq/evaluation/']],[135,230,143])
h('Working principle');para('Check the nominal allowance; apply A and observe; apply B and observe; return to A and observe. Check the complete bracket. Repeat for the configured number of rounds. Always reapply A when leaving the experiment. If every required bracket passes, apply B as the final allocation; otherwise retain A. Failures to actuate or restore must not be reported as successful recovery.')
page('Detailed mechanism');h('7. Description of the invention in detail')
figure('probe')
h('7.1 Observation contract');para('A Window contains a process-incarnation identity, reported effective duty, duration, CPU seconds, protected-service latency samples, offered request rate and health status. It must contain finite values and sufficient observations. The prototype trusts the supplied sampler; a requested duty ratio is not a substitute for measured actuation.')
h('7.2 Acceptance gates');para('All windows must meet the absolute SLO. Offered load must remain stable and the two A-window p95 values must remain close. The B-window p95 increase over the median A-window p95 must remain within its allowance. B CPU seconds divided by B duration times B duty must remain below the demand threshold. A rejected experiment does not prove the process is faulty.')
page('Policy and algorithm');h('7.3 Research configuration')
table(['Parameter','Default'],[['A / B duty in retained simulation','0.15 / 0.40'],['Window / rounds','0.5 seconds / two complete brackets'],['Nominal additional grant budget','0.30 one-core seconds per call'],['Protected p95 / permitted increase','20 ms / 2 ms'],['A-window p95 drift / offered-rate drift','1 ms / 10%'],['Maximum grant-normalized consumption','0.70'],['Minimum latency samples per window','20']],[330,178])
h('7.4 Algorithm');story.append(Preformatted('reserve = (B - A) * window_seconds * rounds\nif reserve > budget: reject before actuation\ntry:\n    for each required round:\n        before = apply_and_observe(A)\n        trial  = apply_and_observe(B)\n        after  = apply_and_observe(A)\n        check validity, load stability and control drift\n        check protected latency and normalized demand\n        if any gate fails: retain restriction\nfinally:\n    apply(A)\nif every complete bracket passed:\n    try: apply(B)\n    on failure: apply(A); raise\nreturn decision, final requested duty, phase trace',mono))
page('Supporting validation');h('7.5 Supporting validation and guarded control');para('The current project supports disjoint train, calibration and test runs. Training/calibration contain normal observations; test data contains both labels. It reports detector errors and agreement, repeats model fits with fixed seeds, and runs randomized-order repeated live benchmark trials. A candidate detector supplements Isolation Forest with a robust normal-training support envelope.')
para('Optional assisted control requires a model hash matching a recent evaluation report, minimum held-out counts and configured quality bounds. ML must corroborate a rule watchlist score for three observations and can only elevate it to soft restriction. It cannot independently authorize restoration or termination. The supplied small dataset fails the deployment gate.')
para('The dashboard defaults to dry-run and loopback binding. Enabled actuation is limited to registered live children, priority changes are disabled in that guarded path, and automatic termination is separately opt-in. An in-process heartbeat lease releases restrictions after expiry. These are supporting implementation features, not a claim that ML and the bracketed runner have been integrated into one controller.')
h('7.6 Limits');para('The nominal grant budget is not a hard real-time bound. An unresponsive sampler, daemon death, failed signal delivery or PID races require stronger external supervision and OS facilities. Bracketing does not prove causality; low grant-normalized consumption may reflect blocking or contention. Cross-platform equivalence, generalization and application-state preservation remain unproven.')
h('7.7 Prepare the screenshot environment');para('Run commands from the project root. The complete project ZIP includes the retained controlled JSONL and evaluated models. A source-only clone requires collecting the labelled file before running SS3; the results will vary and must be shown as produced.')
story.append(Preformatted('python3 -m venv .venv\n.venv/bin/python -m pip install -r requirements-evaluation.txt\n# Only if controlled-labels.jsonl is absent:\nPYTHONPATH=. .venv/bin/python scripts/collect_labelled.py',mono))

page('Measurement definitions');h('7.8 Quantities, units and a worked example')
table(['Quantity','Definition / interpretation'],[['Restricted / candidate duty','A and B are requested execution fractions, with 0 < A < B <= 1 in the nominal one-core model.'],['Normalized trial consumption','u_B = CPU_seconds_B / (duration_B * effective_duty_B). This is a ratio, not a probability of recovery.'],['Additional grant reservation','E = (B - A) * window_seconds * rounds. Units: nominal one-core seconds.'],['Relative latency penalty','p95(B) minus median(p95(A_before), p95(A_after)).'],['Control drift','Absolute difference between the two restricted-window p95 values.'],['Precision / recall','TP/(TP+FP) and TP/(TP+FN); report undefined denominators explicitly.'],['FPR / F1','FP/(FP+TN) and 2TP/(2TP+FP+FN).']],[185,323])
para('For A = 0.15, B = 0.40, 0.5-second windows and two rounds, E = 0.25 nominal core-seconds, below the configured 0.30 allowance. A hypothetical B window using 0.10 CPU-seconds has u_B = 0.50. This passes the 0.70 demand threshold only; every other gate must still pass. These example values are explanatory, not measurements.')
para('Returning to A means reapplying the restriction; it does not restore application memory or rewind execution. The document therefore does not report a snapshot rollback time. Reapplication and confirmed actuator latency need explicit timestamps and a dedicated experiment before numerical claims are made.')
page('Failure handling and integration');h('7.9 Failure handling, integration and technical boundaries')
table(['Condition','Required behavior / limitation'],[['PID incarnation changes','Reject the observation group; never combine telemetry from different process lifetimes.'],['Missing or non-finite observation','Reject as inconclusive; absence of telemetry is not a healthy zero.'],['Load or control drift exceeds bound','Retain the restriction; do not infer recovery from a changing experiment.'],['Protected latency fails a bound','Reject the candidate step even if its normalized CPU demand is low.'],['Sampler or actuation raises','Attempt base reapplication through finally; propagate failure instead of claiming successful recovery.'],['Final relaxation fails','Attempt to reapply A and expose the failure. A second failed actuation requires external intervention.'],['Monitor heartbeat expires','Guarded dashboard path releases managed restrictions; this in-process lease is separate from the research probe.'],['Daemon killed or machine fails','No independent watchdog guarantee is implemented. OS-backed supervision is future work.']],[190,318])
para('The integration boundary matters: bracketed verification is an opt-in API, while dashboard restoration follows the base controller. ML assistance is separately guarded and cannot authorize recovery. An end-to-end policy integrating these paths has not been validated.')
para('Python, native OS telemetry, process signals, standard-library HTTP serving and optional scikit-learn/joblib form the current stack. The prototype is a local research tool, not a replacement kernel scheduler, container security boundary or distributed cluster manager.')

