para('The apparent perfect Extra Trees separation must be read alongside Section 8.11. It is a result for these collection domains, not a validated 100% cryptojacking-detection capability. Both model artifacts explicitly record deployment_eligible = false.')
page('Kaggle interpretation');h('8.11 Collection confounding and deployment boundary')
para('All attack-file observations come from a single host, localhost.localdomain. Normal-file observations come from four other VM hosts: vm1-graph-analytics, vm2-node, vm3-tomcat and vm4-web-server. Their collection dates also differ. Thus labels are confounded with the host and collection period. A model can separate resource distributions associated with these environments without learning a general attack signature.')
para('Removing hostname and timestamp columns does not remove this indirect signal. Memory distributions and CPU states can still reveal collection conditions. Chronological splitting, purging and duplicate removal reduce some leakage risks but do not create an unseen-host attack evaluation. A dataset containing only one attack host cannot support that claim.')
